  partName: Low-Pressure Compressor
  description: The low-pressure compressor is a large, complex component situated
    on the left side of the engine, responsible for compressing air and directing
    it towards the high-pressure compressor. Its plastic-grey material and moderate
    vertex count indicate a balance between durability and weight reduction. The
    low-pressure compressor works in conjunction with the high-pressure compressor
    to achieve optimal compression ratios.
